From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0399-sweep-03-query-dma-wait-only-for-missing.patch

Source: 0399-sweep-03-query-dma-wait-only-for-missing.patch
Moved by hand: without its FrontDmaReadFast hunk: that fast path belongs to the left-out 0353 (EDEN_NX2_DMA_WAIT_WRITERS)

query: EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_SYNC=2 writes landed reports at once and waits only for missing ones

Port of what 0317 (lichii-shaders-0203) lacks from zortos293/Lichii PR 215 (WeslieDE, 9ab3d845b8, on
vouion's #204, 0bdc4ad004, open). GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

The source: Ocarina's leaves and terrain flashed overexposed whenever the camera moved. 976 macro DMA
reads of pending reports in about 2.5 minutes, all macro 0xe2c method 0x158, each read a value other
than the one that landed. With the PR the flashes are gone. Author test only: NVIDIA, Linux, Low.

Same in 0317: EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_TRACE, and a wait that really waits below High accuracy.
SignalAndWait does what the PR's FlushQueryResults does (operation behind the reports, fence, deferred
work submitted, wait), so it is reused. SkipEmptyFence cannot drop that fence: it sees the operation.

Missing from 0317, added here:
- SemiFlushRegion: reports with a final value go to guest memory at once, with no wait.
- The wait only when a report has no host result yet. 0317 waits on anything still registered, and
  nothing sets IsGuestSynced, so it also waits on reports that have landed.
- The hook in macro.cpp, for macros run where the caches are owned. Trace and sync work there now
  too. It only matters with EDEN_NX2_SPLIT below 2, or before the front takes the macros.

Changed from the source: behind the switch, as =2, so =1 stays 0317 and the two can be compared. The
reports go after the buffer cache flush at both sites; the PR does that in FrontDmaRead only, and
goes first in macro.cpp. =2 also turns FrontDmaReadFast off, which would skip the hook under
EDEN_NX2_DMA_WAIT_WRITERS, a path the PR's base does not have.

The wait has no time limit, as in the PR and 0317: if the GPU hangs, the back waits with it. It runs
on the split's back inside a drain, like 0317's. Unset, nothing changes but one comparison per DMA
read. Memory: none. Not run. Syntax checked for the PS5 target only.

